<title>AUSTRIA: Bank Austria sees EPS doubling in next five yrs.</title>
<headline>Bank Austria sees EPS doubling in next five yrs.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Austria, chosen by the Finance Ministry to buy flagship bank Creditanstalt, said on Sunday it expected earnings per share to double in the next five years.</p>
<p>&quot;We are assuming that in the next five years earnings per share double,&quot; Bank Austria chief executive Gerhard Randa told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Bank Austria's earnings per share for 1995 was 43 schillings.</p>
<p>Randa said the bank's parent operating profit for 1996 rose a preliminary five percent to 5.1 billion schillings and that net profit would be a shade lower than the previous year.</p>
<p>He added he did not have the exact figures on a group basis but noted they would show similar fluctuations.</p>
</text>
